# Resource-loading half of the edge Content-Security-Policy.
#
# 40-biotron-sites.sh fills ${BASE_DOMAIN} in the policy line at the bottom
# once per instance in EDGE_SITES and maps each domain to its own policy, so
# every instance names only its own product subdomains. nginx.conf sends the
# mapped value as Content-Security-Policy-Report-Only at http level, beside the
# deployment-independent headers, so they accumulate rather than override each
# other. Lines starting with # are left out of the header.
#
# WHY REPORT-ONLY.
#
# Every frontend except Sprinter carries a synchronous inline theme bootstrap in
# index.html, and AGENTS.md requires it to stay there so the dark theme applies
# before React loads. React also writes inline style attributes throughout. An
# enforced "script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'" would therefore white-flash or
# blank all five apps on first paint. The honest alternatives are per-app script
# hashes -- which this shared edge cannot compute, and which break on every
# index.html edit -- or 'unsafe-inline', which gives back most of what a CSP is
# for. So the policy below is shipped in Report-Only: it is exact about the
# origins the apps legitimately reach, it produces console violations for
# anything else, and it cannot break a page.
#
# TO ENFORCE IT LATER: collect violations from a staging browse of all five apps
# first. Then either give the bootstrap a build-time nonce/hash and drop
# 'unsafe-inline' from script-src, or accept 'unsafe-inline' for script-src and
# rename this header to Content-Security-Policy. Do not enforce it blind.
#
# The directives were derived by reading what the apps actually load:
#   script-src / style-src  inline theme bootstrap and <style> in each
#                           index.html, plus React inline style attributes;
#                           bundles themselves are same-origin Vite output.
#   img-src                 same-origin assets, Vite's inlined data: URIs, and
#                           GitHub avatars (operator.avatar_url is rendered in
#                           the account menu of all four authenticated apps).
#   font-src                Tailwind ships no webfont and no frontend links
#                           Google Fonts; data: covers any future inlined face.
#   connect-src             each frontend calls its own API and, cross-origin,
#                           auth.${BASE_DOMAIN}; the public site calls the
#                           calendar API. Enumerated rather than wildcarded.
#   worker-src blob:        Three.js loaders on the public site construct their
#                           decoder workers from blobs.
#   frame-src 'none'        no frontend embeds an iframe.
default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://avatars.githubusercontent.com; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://${BASE_DOMAIN} https://www.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://auth.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://exogui.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://status.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://calendar.${BASE_DOMAIN} https://sprinter.${BASE_DOMAIN}; worker-src 'self' blob:; frame-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'none'; object-src 'none'; form-action 'self'
